## FRONTEND ARCHITECTURE

### Q: How does routing work?

**A:** I use **TanStack Router** with file-based routing. Each file in `src/routes/` automatically becomes a route:
- [index.tsx](file:///c:/Users/rahul/OneDrive/Booksubmission_grp2/manuscript-buddy/src/routes/index.tsx) → `/` (login page)
- [dashboard.tsx](file:///c:/Users/rahul/OneDrive/Booksubmission_grp2/manuscript-buddy/src/routes/dashboard.tsx) → `/dashboard` (author home)
- [submit.tsx](file:///c:/Users/rahul/OneDrive/Booksubmission_grp2/manuscript-buddy/src/routes/submit.tsx) → `/submit` (submission wizard)
- [editor.tsx](file:///c:/Users/rahul/OneDrive/Booksubmission_grp2/manuscript-buddy/src/routes/editor.tsx) → `/editor` (editor review queue)
- [admin.tsx](file:///c:/Users/rahul/OneDrive/Booksubmission_grp2/manuscript-buddy/src/routes/admin.tsx) → `/admin` (admin panel)
- [manuscript.$id.tsx](file:///c:/Users/rahul/OneDrive/Booksubmission_grp2/manuscript-buddy/src/routes/manuscript.$id.tsx) → `/manuscript/:id` (dynamic route for manuscript detail)
- [analytics.tsx](file:///c:/Users/rahul/OneDrive/Booksubmission_grp2/manuscript-buddy/src/routes/analytics.tsx) → `/analytics`
- [settings.tsx](file:///c:/Users/rahul/OneDrive/Booksubmission_grp2/manuscript-buddy/src/routes/settings.tsx) → `/settings`
- [__root.tsx](file:///c:/Users/rahul/OneDrive/Booksubmission_grp2/manuscript-buddy/src/routes/__root.tsx) → the root layout wrapping all routes (provides HTML shell, QueryClient, AppProvider, Toaster)

### Q: How do you manage global state?

**A:** I use **React Context API** with a custom [AppProvider](file:///c:/Users/rahul/OneDrive/Booksubmission_grp2/manuscript-buddy/src/store/app-store.tsx#29-122). It holds:
- `user` — the logged-in user object (name, email, role)
- [manuscripts](file:///c:/Users/rahul/OneDrive/Booksubmission_grp2/manuscript-buddy/erpnext_backend/manuscript_management/api.py#108-147) — the full list of manuscripts loaded from the backend
- `loading` / `error` — UI states
- [login()](file:///c:/Users/rahul/OneDrive/Booksubmission_grp2/manuscript-buddy/src/services/erpnextClient.ts#114-145), [logout()](file:///c:/Users/rahul/OneDrive/Booksubmission_grp2/manuscript-buddy/src/services/erpnextClient.ts#146-153), `refresh()` — action functions

Every page accesses this via the [useApp()](file:///c:/Users/rahul/OneDrive/Booksubmission_grp2/manuscript-buddy/src/store/app-store.tsx#123-128) hook. When the user logs in, a `useEffect` detects the user change and automatically calls `refresh()` which fetches all manuscripts from the backend. After any mutation (submit, decision, state change), I call `refresh()` to re-fetch the latest data.

### Q: Why React Context instead of Redux or Zustand?

**A:** The app has a simple, flat state shape — just a user object and a manuscripts list. React Context is lightweight, has no extra dependencies, and is sufficient for this use case. Redux would be overkill since I don't have complex state update patterns or deeply nested state. If the app scaled significantly, I could migrate to Zustand or TanStack Query for server state management.

### Q: How does the submission wizard work?

**A:** The submission is a **5-step wizard** built in [submit.tsx](file:///c:/Users/rahul/OneDrive/Booksubmission_grp2/manuscript-buddy/src/routes/submit.tsx):
1. **Title & Category** — Title (max 120 chars), primary genre (8 options), secondary genre, target audience, keywords (tag input with Enter/comma to add).
2. **Description** — Executive abstract (min 5 words), detailed synopsis, estimated page count, target launch date.
3. **Upload PDF** — Drag & drop or click to upload. Only `.pdf` files accepted, max 50MB. A simulated progress bar shows the upload.
4. **Preview & AI Scan** — Left panel shows the PDF in an iframe. Right panel shows the AI Pre-flight Report with scores for readability, marketability, genre confidence, pacing, and an overall score.
5. **Confirm** — Summary of all fields. Author must check an "I confirm this is my original work" checkbox before submitting.

Each step has its own validation. The "Continue" button doesn't proceed unless validation passes. Final submission opens a confirmation dialog, then calls [createManuscript()](file:///c:/Users/rahul/OneDrive/Booksubmission_grp2/manuscript-buddy/src/services/manuscriptService.ts#126-153) on the backend.

### Q: How does the AI analysis work?

**A:** Currently, the AI report is generated **client-side** using the [generateAIReport()](file:///c:/Users/rahul/OneDrive/Booksubmission_grp2/manuscript-buddy/src/services/manuscriptService.ts#95-125) function. It produces randomized scores for:
- **Overall AI score** (62–93%)
- **Genre confidence** — percentage split between primary and secondary genres
- **Readability** (55–94)
- **Marketability** (50–94)
- **Pacing** — per-act scores for Act I, II, III

There's also a **server-side version** ([generate_ai_report](file:///c:/Users/rahul/OneDrive/Booksubmission_grp2/manuscript-buddy/erpnext_backend/manuscript_management/api.py#294-327) in [api.py](file:///c:/Users/rahul/OneDrive/Booksubmission_grp2/manuscript-buddy/erpnext_backend/manuscript_management/api.py)) that does the same thing. In production, this would be replaced with a real NLP/ML pipeline that analyses the manuscript text.

### Q: How does the editor review process work?

**A:** The editor sees a review queue at `/editor` showing all manuscripts with state "Pending Editor Review" or "AI Processing". They can sort by submission date, author, or AI score, and paginate (5 per page). For each manuscript, they can click "Make Decision" which opens a dialog with three options:
- **Approve** — no extra input needed, sets state to "Approved"
- **Request Revisions** — requires a feedback textarea explaining what changes are needed, sets state to "Revisions Requested"
- **Reject** — requires selecting a rejection reason from a predefined list AND writing an explanation, sets state to "Rejected"

The form uses **Zod schema validation** with `superRefine` for conditional validation — feedback is required only for revisions and rejection, and rejection reason is required only for rejection.

### Q: What can the admin do?

**A:** The admin page at `/admin` has:
- **Overview section** — Pipeline stage breakdown with counts, quick-action cards, deadline tracking
- **Manuscripts table** — All manuscripts with search, filter by pipeline stage, sort
- **Actions per manuscript**: Assign/change editor (dropdown), Force-advance to any state, Publish (one-click for approved manuscripts)
- **Manuscript drawer** — Click any row to open a slide-over panel with full details

