## TYPE SAFETY & VALIDATION

### Q: How do you ensure type safety?

**A:** The entire frontend is in **TypeScript**. I have a dedicated [types.ts](file:///c:/Users/rahul/OneDrive/Booksubmission_grp2/manuscript-buddy/src/services/types.ts) file that defines:
- [Role](file:///c:/Users/rahul/OneDrive/Booksubmission_grp2/manuscript-buddy/src/services/types.ts#1-2) type: `"author" | "editor" | "admin"`
- [WorkflowState](file:///c:/Users/rahul/OneDrive/Booksubmission_grp2/manuscript-buddy/src/services/types.ts#12-13) type: a union of all 7 states
- [Manuscript](file:///c:/Users/rahul/OneDrive/Booksubmission_grp2/manuscript-buddy/src/services/types.ts#90-98) type: a **discriminated union** on the [state](file:///c:/Users/rahul/OneDrive/Booksubmission_grp2/manuscript-buddy/erpnext_backend/manuscript_management/api.py#206-216) field — this means TypeScript enforces that `rejectionReason` is only present when `state === "Rejected"`
- Interfaces for [AIReport](file:///c:/Users/rahul/OneDrive/Booksubmission_grp2/manuscript-buddy/src/services/types.ts#28-38), [TimelineEvent](file:///c:/Users/rahul/OneDrive/Booksubmission_grp2/manuscript-buddy/src/services/types.ts#14-20), [EditorNote](file:///c:/Users/rahul/OneDrive/Booksubmission_grp2/manuscript-buddy/src/services/types.ts#21-27), [ListManuscriptsOptions](file:///c:/Users/rahul/OneDrive/Booksubmission_grp2/manuscript-buddy/src/services/types.ts#103-109), `Paginated<T>`, [User](file:///c:/Users/rahul/OneDrive/Booksubmission_grp2/manuscript-buddy/src/services/types.ts#121-126)

### Q: What is the discriminated union pattern you used?

**A:** Instead of having one big [Manuscript](file:///c:/Users/rahul/OneDrive/Booksubmission_grp2/manuscript-buddy/src/services/types.ts#90-98) interface with optional `rejectionReason`, I created separate interfaces for each state (e.g., [DraftManuscript](file:///c:/Users/rahul/OneDrive/Booksubmission_grp2/manuscript-buddy/src/services/types.ts#66-69), [RejectedManuscript](file:///c:/Users/rahul/OneDrive/Booksubmission_grp2/manuscript-buddy/src/services/types.ts#84-89)). Only [RejectedManuscript](file:///c:/Users/rahul/OneDrive/Booksubmission_grp2/manuscript-buddy/src/services/types.ts#84-89) requires `rejectionReason: string`. The [Manuscript](file:///c:/Users/rahul/OneDrive/Booksubmission_grp2/manuscript-buddy/src/services/types.ts#90-98) type is the union of all these. This means if I narrow the type with `if (m.state === "Rejected")`, TypeScript knows `m.rejectionReason` exists and is a string. There's also a helper [isRejected(m)](file:///c:/Users/rahul/OneDrive/Booksubmission_grp2/manuscript-buddy/src/services/types.ts#99-102) type guard function.

### Q: How do you validate forms?

**A:** Two approaches:
1. **Manual validation** (submission wizard in [submit.tsx](file:///c:/Users/rahul/OneDrive/Booksubmission_grp2/manuscript-buddy/src/routes/submit.tsx)): Each step has a [validateStep()](file:///c:/Users/rahul/OneDrive/Booksubmission_grp2/manuscript-buddy/src/routes/submit.tsx#134-151) function that checks required fields and word counts, populating an `errors` object that renders inline error messages.
2. **Zod schema validation** (editor decision dialog in [editor.tsx](file:///c:/Users/rahul/OneDrive/Booksubmission_grp2/manuscript-buddy/src/routes/editor.tsx)): I define a Zod schema with `superRefine` for conditional rules (feedback required if revising, both reason and feedback required if rejecting). React Hook Form integrates with Zod via the `@hookform/resolvers/zod` adapter.

