## SSR & ERROR HANDLING

### Q: Does your app support server-side rendering?

**A:** Yes. TanStack Start provides SSR out of the box via the **Nitro** runtime. The [server.ts](file:///c:/Users/rahul/OneDrive/Booksubmission_grp2/manuscript-buddy/src/server.ts) file is the server entry point — it imports the TanStack Start server module, forwards all requests through it, and handles edge cases like h3 framework swallowing errors into generic JSON responses. If SSR fails, it returns a static HTML error page instead of crashing.

### Q: How do you handle errors in the app?

**A:** Multiple levels:
1. **Root error boundary** in [__root.tsx](file:///c:/Users/rahul/OneDrive/Booksubmission_grp2/manuscript-buddy/src/routes/__root.tsx) — catches any unhandled React error and shows a "This page didn't load" screen with "Try again" and "Go home" buttons
2. **404 handler** — custom Not Found component at the root route level
3. **API errors** — [FrappeError](file:///c:/Users/rahul/OneDrive/Booksubmission_grp2/manuscript-buddy/src/services/erpnextClient.ts#24-37) class parses Frappe error responses; each page handles these with toast notifications or inline error messages
4. **SSR errors** — [server.ts](file:///c:/Users/rahul/OneDrive/Booksubmission_grp2/manuscript-buddy/src/server.ts) catches h3 swallowed errors (HTTP 500 with `{unhandled: true}`) and renders a fallback HTML page
5. **Loading states** — every page shows a spinner while data is loading

